        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(clickclack): wrap websocket message rejections with Error for diagnostics",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe websocket message handler in ClickClack's gateway uses `.catch(reject)` to\nforward errors from the async message processor. When the processor throws a\nnon-Error value (a plain string, `undefined`, or a deserialized error from a\nremote system), the raw rejection loses the stack trace and makes downstream\nerror diagnostics unreliable.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nReplace `.catch(reject)` with an explicit catch block that preserves Error\ninstances and wraps non-Error values with `new Error(\"ClickClack ws message failed\", { cause: e })`.\n\n## Evidence\n\nTests pass:\n\n```text\n$ pnpm test extensions/clickclack/src/gateway.test.ts\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  5 passed (5)\n```\n\nReal behavior proof — the exact patched `gateway.ts:209` catch path wraps\nnon-Error values into diagnostic Error instances with the literal message\n\"ClickClack ws message failed\" and the original value as `cause`:\n\n```text\n$ node proof-clickclack-gateway.mjs\nplain-string: instanceof=true hasCause=true message=\"ClickClack ws message failed\" cause=connection reset\nnumber: instanceof=true hasCause=true message=\"ClickClack ws message failed\" cause=503\nobject: instanceof=true hasCause=true message=\"ClickClack ws message failed\" cause={\"detail\":\"timeout\"}\nexisting-Error: instanceof=true hasCause=false message=\"real err\" cause=none\nDONE: ClickClack ws message failed proof\n```\n\nAI-assisted: built with Codex\n",
        "branch": "sunlit/fix/clickclack-rejection",
        "head_sha": "3b072ee4a4358369e41179f89f3aadc2b91ceea9",
